    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Country/Region of Origin: Afghanistan\nTime Period: 20th century\nHistorical Development: Learned by Gyula Zsigri from Sherzod Lukmoni in 1992. A similar game called Ramchi was described in 2011 by Tilman Schieber, said to have come from Pakistan where it is popular with Afghan refugees.\nCultural Significance: Played in Afghanistan and by Afghan refugee communities in Pakistan.',
